Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: In any oblique triangle the altitude h from the apex gives the height used in area and sine-rule formulas, but when the angle at α is obtuse that altitude falls outside the triangle onto an extension of the base, where the supplementary angle α′ is the one adjacent to the perpendicular.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): The height of a triangle is measured to the line containing the base, not to the base segment itself — so h = c·sin α works for obtuse triangles too, because the exterior angle α′ that actually forms the right triangle has exactly the same sine as α.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

